1220
00:53:20.380 --> 00:53:22.620
I was like, oh, Ed, that is so sweet.

1221
00:53:23.120 --> 00:53:28.800
And so we literally did, you know, what we call like grandparent kissing where you're just like, mm.

1222
00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:32.740
He did not open his lips for a second.

1223
00:53:32.920 --> 00:53:37.780
And they really wanted me to sort of have this long kiss, right?

1224
00:53:37.940 --> 00:53:38.160
Yeah.

1225
00:53:38.300 --> 00:53:39.240
And I was in control.

1226
00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:42.580
I was the one that grabbed him and then I was the one that released him.

1227
00:53:42.760 --> 00:53:46.240
And I remember one time they were like, can you sell it a little bit more?

1228
00:53:46.340 --> 00:53:47.800
Can you make it a little bit bigger of a moment?

1229
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:53.120
And poor Ed, the minute we broke apart, he went, oh, because he hadn't been breathing?

1230
00:53:53.400 --> 00:53:57.400
He was holding his breath with a big bite of tuna fish sandwich in his mouth.

1231
00:53:57.400 --> 00:53:58.860
Here's my question.

1232
00:53:59.200 --> 00:54:01.600
Couldn't Phil have made fakie tuna fish?

1233
